# Measured 2026-09-16 against Xvfb 2:21.1.22-1ubuntu1 on :95 and 2026-09-17
# against Xwayland 24.1.10 (2:24.1.10-1) on :0 under headless sway 1.11, both
# from a raw socket with scripts/xw11-probe-bigreq.py; the Xwayland probe was
# run twice, byte-identical, and all six blocks matched Xvfb's byte for byte.
# Same shape as its two siblings -- setup, QueryExtension, Enable, then the probe
# as request 3 -- but line 1 is a big-form GetProperty claiming ZERO words, which
# is block (b) of the probe's output. Xwayland 24.1.10 did the same on
# 2026-09-17: a zero-byte read, the connection closed.
# There is no line 2, and that is the measurement: the server sent NOTHING and
# closed the connection. The read came back zero bytes, no BadLength, no error
# of any kind, and the four NoOperations and the GetInputFocus behind the probe
# went nowhere. A zero there is the one big form the server will not answer for,
# which is why xw11/wire.py answers BAD_LENGTH_CLOSE rather than BAD_LENGTH.
1400000000000000
